{"batchcomplete": true, "query": {"pages": [{"pageid": 229497, "ns": 0, "title": "Acre (state)", "extract": "Acre (, AH-krə; Portuguese: [ˈakɾi] ) is a state located in the west of the North Region of Brazil and the Amazonia Legal. Located in the westernmost part of the country, at a two-hour time difference from Brasília, Acre is bordered clockwise by the Brazilian states of Amazonas and Rondônia to the north and east, along with an international border with the Bolivian department of Pando to the southeast, and the Peruvian regions of Madre de Dios, Ucayali and Loreto to the south and west. Its capital and largest city is Rio Branco. Other important places include Cruzeiro do Sul, Sena Madureira, Tarauacá and Feijó. The state, which has 0.42% of the Brazilian population, generates 0.2% of the Brazilian GDP.\nIntense extractive activity in the rubber industry, which reached its height in the early 20th century, attracted Brazilians from many regions to the state. From the mixture of sulista, southeastern Brazil, nordestino, and indigenous traditions arose a diverse cuisine.\nFluvial transport, concentrated on the Juruá and Moa rivers, in the western part of the state, and the Tarauacá and Envira rivers in the northwest, is the principal form of transportation, especially between November and June. Heavy seasonal rains frequently make the BR-364 impassable in those months; it usually connects Rio Branco to Cruzeiro do Sul.", "contentmodel": "wikitext", "pagelanguage": "en", "pagelanguagehtmlcode": "en", "pagelanguagedir": "ltr", "touched": "2026-08-06T16:19:14Z", "lastrevid": 1365403755, "length": 60128, "fullurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acre_(state)", "editurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Acre_(state)&action=edit", "canonicalurl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acre_(state)", "pageprops": {"wikibase_item": "Q40780"}, "coordinates": [{"lat": -9, "lon": -70, "primary": true, "globe": "earth"}], "extlinks": [{"url": "http://www.worldwildlife.o